OL,3,GNEWSAHow can heritage buildings be
OL,4,Abrought back into use?
OL,5,
OL,6,FA hotel which was used by pilgrims
OL,7,Fvisiting the tomb of Edward II has been
OL,8,Fgiven government funding for
OL,9,Frenovation.
OL,11,FThe Fleece Hotel, in Gloucester, was
OL,12,Fvisited by a host of famous faces in
OL,13,Fits heyday, including former UK Prime
OL,14,FMinister Margaret Thatcher, actress
OL,15,FGracie Fields and British intelligence
OL,16,Fofficer and double agent Kim Philby.
OL,18,FThe historic hotel, in Westgate Street,
OL,19,Fhas been closed since 2002 despite
OL,20,Fvarious efforts to reopen it.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
